---
title: "Get the authenticated account"
icon: arrow-down-left
description: "Get the authenticated account: getAccount in the TypeScript, Python and Rust clients."
---

`GET /v1/account`

Returns the profile of the authenticated account. The account is selected from the credential rather than a request parameter. A missing or deleted account is reported as an error instead of an empty profile.

<Tabs>
<Tab title="TypeScript">
```typescript TypeScript
photon.account.get(input?: GetAccountInput, options?: RequestOptions): Promise<GetAccountOutput>
```
</Tab>
<Tab title="Python">
```python Python
photon.account.get(input: GetAccountInput | None = None) -> models.Account
```
</Tab>
<Tab title="Rust">
```rust Rust
client.get_account().await -> Result<ResponseValue<types::Account>, Error<GetAccountError>>
```
</Tab>
</Tabs>

<RequestExample>
```typescript TypeScript
import { Photon } from "@photon-ai/api";

const photon = new Photon({
  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.PHOTON_API_TOKEN}` },
});
const result = await photon.account.get();
```

```python Python
import os

from photon_api import Photon

photon = Photon(headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {os.environ['PHOTON_API_TOKEN']}"})
result = photon.account.get()
```

```rust Rust
use photon_ai_api::{Credential, PhotonClientBuilder, SecretString};

let token = std::env::var("PHOTON_API_TOKEN")?;
let client = PhotonClientBuilder::new()
    .credential("accountServiceKey", Credential::Bearer(SecretString::from(token)))
    .build()?;
let result = client
    .get_account()
    .await
    .map_err(|error| format!("{error:?}"))?
    .into_inner();
```

</RequestExample>

<ResponseExample>
```json 200
{
  "accountId": "string",
  "createdAt": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "firstName": null,
  "lastName": null,
  "phoneNumber": null,
  "phoneVerifiedAt": null,
  "pictureUrl": "https://example.com",
  "updatedAt": null
}
```

</ResponseExample>

